oin="round" version="1.1" class="svgicon icon_map" aria-hidden="" fill="none"><polygon points="1 6 1 22 8 18 16 22 23 18 23 2 16 6 8 2 1 6"></polygon><line x1="8" y1="2" x2="8" y2="18"></line><line x1="16" y1="6" x2="16" y2="22"></line></svg> <span class="full_label">More like this</span><span class="mobile_label">Related</span></a></li></ul><div id="wrapper" class="main wrapper game_page_wrapper"><div id="inner_column" class="inner_column size_large family_lato" style="min-height: 959px;"><div id="header" class="header"><h1 itemprop="name" class="game_title">Low Poly Bedroom Asset Pack</h1></div><div id="view_game_8745161" class="view_game_page page_widget base_widget buy_on_top" tabindex="-1"><div class="header_buy_row"><p>A downloadable asset pack</p><div class="buy_row"><div class="button_message"><a href="https://kyle-fuji.itch.io/low-poly-bedroom-asset-pack/purchase" class="button buy_btn">Download Now</a><span class="buy_message"><span class="sub">Name your own price</span></span></div></div></div><div class="columns"><div class="left_col column"><div class="formatted_description user_formatted"><p>I made this to practice making game assets from blender. I've taken a break from making game assets, and decided to return to it with a free bedroom asset pack! I wanted to make it be very easy to customize, while being simple and low poly. All dressers and drawers are using a basic wood material I added, but you can change it to be anything you want! I even added some example images showing different lights and materials customized. Drawers can be opened and closed as well with their own animations!</p>
<p>I added versions that work on Unity 6.2 (URP) and Godot 4.5, as well as the fbx files and the maps required to import it to any other game engine or render pipeline!</p>
<p>Screenshots taken in Godot. However, they&nbsp;look just as good, if not better in Unity.</p>
